**About the Position:** The Login Clerk 2 is responsible for sample receipt and log\-in, client services, data entry, and sample subletting as well as bottle preparation.


**Specific Responsibilities**

* Accepts samples and accurately processes cash payments in accordance with internal accounting practices for sample processing from private clients, enters all payments into the appropriate file
* Labeling select workorders under supervision
* Accurate Data entry of all Chain of Custody information into internal Laboratory Information Management System (LIMS);
* Provides assistance and feedback to clients regarding basic questions arising in sample receipt area;
* Receive work orders as they arrive in the laboratory \& performs sample triage;
* Open and layout samples and paperwork to confirm all required samples have been received;
* Enters client account number, project for billing and contact information in sample login screen;
* Enter analytical codes for samples;
* Familiarity with all ALS location turnaround times (TAT’s);
* Transport samples into lab;
* Clean, organize and distribute coolers as needed;
* Ensure adherence to all procedures and policies (safety, quality, employment and technical);
* Train other staff;
* Follow safety requirements in Safety Manual \& communicate all safety concerns/incidents to Safety Rep;
* Observe established safety regulations and comply with all ALS health and safety policies and procedures;
* Other duties as assigned.

**Required Knowledge, Skills \& Abilities**

* Good English communication skills required (auditory, verbal, written, and reading);
* Intermediate user of Microsoft Office (Word and Outlook), with basic knowledge of computers;
* Must have good organizational skills and be able to handle a fluctuating work load and prioritize work with great attention to detail;
* Excellent customer services skills, verbal skills including telephone answering;
* Must be capable of working with minimal supervision;
* Must be well organized and able to work independently, as well as part of a team.

**Required Qualifications**

* Completion of high school diploma or equivalent required;
* Experience in Customer Service including cash handling;
* BSc or Technical Diploma in Environmental Science or Chemistry an asset;

**Physical Demands**

* Manual dexterity to perform intricate and/or repetitive tasks;
* Wear issued personal protective equipment (PPE) as required;
* Ability to lift up to 30 lbs./14 kg on a regular basis and carry for short distances;
* Ability to sit or stand for a full shift;
* You may be exposed to unpleasant odours;
* Please note that ALS operates 24/7 and will require day, afternoon, and graveyard shift work including weekends .

