**Position Summary:** 

Reporting to the Executive Director, the Business Operations Administrator is responsible for the day\-to\-day administration of the organization’s cross\-functional operations including human resources support, finance support and business development support. The Business Operations Administrator will serve as an assistant to the Executive Director and as the primary administrative resource to the CDIC Board of Directors and its standing committees. In addition to human resources and finance support, the position leads governance administration — meeting coordination, agendas, minutes, motions, resolutions and corporate records — and administers CDIC’s HubSpot CRM in support of business development and marketing activities. The Business Operations Administrator plays a key role in the successful operation of the business, works closely with the Executive Director on confidential and time\-sensitive matters, and coordinates team building activities to maintain an exceptional corporate culture.

**Duties and Responsibilities:**

**Executive Assistance \& Board Governance Support:** 

· Manages the Executive Director’s priorities and deadlines, tracking commitments and following up with internal and external parties on the Executive Director’s behalf;

· Serves as the primary administrative contact for the CDIC Board of Directors and its standing committees;

· Coordinates the annual Board and committee meeting calendar; prepares, assembles and circulates agendas, meeting packages and supporting materials in advance of each meeting;

· Records, drafts and distributes minutes for Board and committee meetings, including in camera sessions, applying Robert’s Rules of Order and maintaining strict confidentiality;

· Tracks motions, resolutions and action items arising from Board and committee meetings and follows up to ensure completion;

· Drafts member and Board resolutions, director appointment documentation, and other governance records for review by the Executive Director;

· Maintains the corporate governance record, including by\-laws, policies, board and committee rosters, conflict of interest declarations, director records and contact information, and executed resolutions;

· Assists the Executive Director with the annual general meeting, strategic planning sessions, and reporting on progress against the strategic plan and associated key performance indicators;

**Business Development, Marketing \& CRM Administration:** 

· Serves as the account administrator for CDIC’s HubSpot CRM, including user management, permissions, system configuration, and data quality and integrity;

